# Engram + OpenSpec (RHCL)

Engram MCP is available (project binding is **per-developer** via local `.engram/config.json`, gitignored). Use it proactively — the user must not need to ask.

## Authority (non-negotiable)

| Knowledge | Authoritative store | Engram |
|-----------|---------------------|--------|
| Specs, tasks, acceptance criteria, change artifacts | `openspec/changes/` → archive to `openspec/specs/` | Never substitute |
| New SDD work | OpenSpec only (`/opsx-propose` … `/opsx-archive`) | Do not use legacy `sdd/{change}/*` Engram-only workflow |
| Standards, backlog | `docs/base-standards.md`, `docs/sdd-backlog.md` | Link only; do not duplicate full text |
| **Design / architecture decisions** | **`design.md` (and related OpenSpec artifacts) in the SDD store** | **Also `mem_save` (dual-write)** |
| Session gotchas, CI/workflow, preferences, PR patterns | Engram | Primary |
| Code structure | CodeGraph + repo | Engram for *why*, not *where* |

See `docs/sdd-backlog.md` (Engram migration) and product `AGENTS.md` (SDD section).

## Dual-write for design and architecture

When a **design or architecture decision** is made or updated:

1. **SDD first** — record it in the active change’s `design.md` (or propose/update via OpenSpec workflow). That is the team-facing source of truth.
2. **Engram second** — `mem_save` with:
   - `type`: `architecture` or `decision`
   - `topic_key`: `rhcl/architecture/<stable-slug>` (reuse to update the same topic)
   - `content`: What / Why / Where — include the **OpenSpec path** (e.g. `openspec/changes/foo/design.md`) so memory points to the canonical doc

If the decision exists only in Engram, it is incomplete — fix the SDD artifact.

## When to save (agent-initiated)

Call `mem_save` after: bugfix, design/architecture decision (after SDD write), non-obvious discovery, config/setup, established pattern, user preference.

Use `mem_suggest_topic_key` when unsure; reuse keys for evolving topics.

## When to search (agent-initiated)

At start of related work: `mem_context`, then `mem_search` if needed. On recall requests (“remember”, “recordar”, etc.): `mem_context` → `mem_search` → `mem_get_observation`.

For architecture questions, prefer OpenSpec `design.md` + Engram search together — SDD wins on conflict.

## Session close

Before ending substantial work: `mem_session_summary` (Goal, Discoveries, Accomplished, Next Steps, Relevant Files).

After compaction: `mem_session_summary` first, then `mem_context`.
